    "explanation": "Both sides' evidence agrees on what decides this case, so the outcome is the same however the parties frame it.\n\nThe driver tapped 'I'm Here' at 12:51:17 and the platform started a 180-second free waiting period at 12:51:19 (EV-TRIP-02706, platform_policy.free_wait_sec = 180 s). He cancelled at 12:52:28, and his own GPS trace shows one continuous in-geofence run of 67 seconds, from 12:51:17 to 12:52:24, on 8 qualifying fixes (EV-GPS-02706, derived.arrival.longest_qualifying_run.duration_sec = 67 s; derived.arrival.shortfall_sec = 113 s). The trip record's own wait timer tells the same story: 69 seconds of waiting against 180 seconds required. POL-NS-01 limb (c) therefore fails - the driver did not hold position for the free waiting period in force - and limb (d) fails with it, because the trip was not terminated at or after the moment the required dwell elapsed. The fee was not earned under POL-NS-01.\n\nPOL-NS-06 then governs the refund: where the effective in-geofence dwell is shorter than the waiting period in force, the cancellation fee is not chargeable and is refunded to the rider in full, whether or not the rider was present and whether or not she responded to messages. The rider's message 'im at the lobby, coming out' at 12:52:17 and her track (39 fixes within 13-19 m of the pin) are consistent with that but are not needed for it. The fare ledger (EV-FARE-02706) shows the SGD 4.50 cancellation-fee line charged at 12:52:45 with payment_status CHARGED and refund_issued_sgd 0.00, and that is the sum refunded.\n\nThe driver cannot top up his dwell by summing separate intervals: under POL-NS-06(i) that route requires a present and populated traffic advisory, and EV-ADVIS-02706-01 is MISSING (weight 0.0), so limb (i) is unavailable and no separate intervals can be added. Two claims on that point were discarded at the mechanical check (a zero-weight artifact was cited without naming the MISSING_ARTIFACT issue code).\n\nOn the claim that POL-NS-04 exonerates the rider: it is not needed and does not decide this case. The outcome it would produce - full refund with no driver compensation - is the outcome POL-NS-06 already produces on the dwell arithmetic. I note only that the driver's single chat reply 'ok' was posted at 12:52:32, four seconds after he had already cancelled at 12:52:28.\n\nOn driver compensation: none is payable. POL-NS-07 pays only where POL-NS-01 is satisfied in full, and it is not. The anti-farming check does not trip (EV-DPROF-02706: no_show_terminations_30d = 0 against completed_trips_30d = 107), which is in the driver's favour but cannot create a payout where the waiting period the fee buys was never served.\n\nOn the counterparty statement ('Rider was not visible and I had another booking waiting'): it is the driver's own account that he had somewhere else to be, and it is consistent with his early cancellation, but it changes nothing above; and carrying no weight_multiplier it does not move the confidence cap in either direction.\n\nNo escalation. POL-NS-09 is not engaged: confidence is above the 0.70 floor, no two admissible artifacts contradict each other on arrival, dwell or rider presence, neither profile shows the repeat-abuse or anti-farming pattern (EV-RPROF-02706: no_show_disputes_30d = 0, disputes_with_counterparty_90d = 0; EV-DPROF-02706: disputes_with_counterparty_90d = 0, no_show_terminations_30d = 0), and no deciding fact rests on an impaired artifact. The arrival marker is not false under POL-NS-05 - at 12:51:17 the driver's own trace places him inside the 50 m STANDARD radius - so no false-arrival referral is generated, and no other clause produces a referral.\n\nConfidence. The deciding fact - a 67-second dwell against a 180-second minimum - is carried by EV-GPS-02706 and EV-TRIP-02706, both at weight_multiplier 1.0, and they independently agree. The POL-GEN-02(2) cap is therefore 1.0, and I set confidence at 0.95, above the 0.70 floor.\n\nThe monetary effect, SGD 4.50, is below the POL-GEN-05 execution threshold of SGD 8.00, so it executes automatically on issue. The outcome is FULL_REFUND of SGD 4.50 to the rider, with no driver compensation."
