    "explanation": "To the rider and the driver: the SGD 4.50 no-show cancellation fee charged on trip TRP-02706 is refunded in full to the rider, and no driver compensation is payable.\n\nWhy the fee does not stand. A no-show fee is chargeable only if every limb of POL-NS-01 holds. The driver did tap 'I'm Here' at 12:51:17 (EV-TRIP-02706) and the GPS trace (EV-GPS-02706) does place him inside the 50 m STANDARD pickup geofence at that moment, so limbs (a) and (b) are met. But the trace shows him holding position inside the geofence for only 67 continuous seconds, from 12:51:17 to 12:52:24, across 8 qualifying fixes. The free waiting period in force for this trip is 180 seconds (trip_record.platform_policy.free_wait_sec, EV-TRIP-02706), so the dwell falls 113 seconds short - the shortfall figure EV-GPS-02706 itself reports. The platform's own wait timer started at 12:51:19 and the driver cancelled at 12:52:28, 69 seconds later. POL-NS-01(c) therefore fails, and under POL-NS-06 the cancellation fee is not chargeable and is refunded in full, whether or not the rider was present and whether or not she responded to messages. The fare ledger (EV-FARE-02706) shows SGD 4.50 charged at 12:52:45 with payment_status CHARGED and refund_issued_sgd 0.00; that is the figure returned.\n\nNo driver compensation. POL-NS-07 pays the driver only where POL-NS-01 is satisfied in full, and it is not. The anti-farming check does not trip either: EV-DPROF-02706 shows no_show_terminations_30d of 0 against completed_trips_30d of 107.\n\nThe arrival marker is not false. At 12:51:17 the driver was already inside the geofence and stationary, so the waiting clock is not recomputed under POL-NS-05 and no false-arrival referral arises.\n\nThe driver's statement that 'Rider was not visible and I had another booking waiting' does not save the fee. The charge does not turn on whether the rider was visible; it turns on the driver serving out the waiting period, which the trace shows he did not. For com